{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nAlice has got addicted to a game called Sirtet recently.In Sirtet, player is given an $$$n \\times m$$$ grid. Initially $$$a_{i,j}$$$ cubes are stacked up in the cell $$$(i,j)$$$. Two cells are called adjacent if they share a side. Player can perform the following operations:   stack up one cube in two adjacent cells;  stack up two cubes in one cell. Cubes mentioned above are identical in height.Here is an illustration of the game. States on the right are obtained by performing one of the above operations on the state on the left, and grey cubes are added due to the operation.  Player's goal is to make the height of all cells the same (i.e. so that each cell has the same number of cubes in it) using above operations. Alice, however, has found out that on some starting grids she may never reach the goal no matter what strategy she uses. Thus, she is wondering the number of initial grids such that   $$$L \\le a_{i,j} \\le R$$$ for all $$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$, $$$1 \\le j \\le m$$$;  player can reach the goal using above operations. Please help Alice with it. Notice that the answer might be large, please output the desired value modulo $$$998,244,353$$$.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class E {\n    static final long MOD = 998244353;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner in = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = in.nextLong();\n        long m = in.nextLong();\n        long p = in.nextLong();\n        long q = in.nextLong();\n        long total = q - p + 1;\n        long odd = (p % 2 == 1) ? (total + 1) / 2 : total / 2;\n        long even = total - odd;\n        long cells = n * m;\n        if ((n & m) % 2 == 0) {\n            System.out.println(computeEven(odd, even, cells));\n        } else {\n            System.out.println(computeOdd(odd + even, cells));\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static long computeEven(long odd, long even, long n) {\n        if (n == 0) return 1;\n        if (n == 1) return odd;\n        long[] state = {odd, even};\n        long[][] trans = {{odd, even}, {even, odd}};\n        long[][] powered = matrixExp(trans, n - 1);\n        return (powered[0][0] * state[0] + powered[0][1] * state[1]) % MOD;\n    }\n\n    private static long[][] matrixExp(long[][] base, long exp) {\n        long[][] result = {{1, 0}, {0, 1}};\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) result = matMul(result, base);\n            base = matMul(base, base);\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    private static long[][] matMul(long[][] a, long[][] b) {\n        long[][] c = new long[2][2];\n        for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < 2; j++) {\n                c[i][j] = 0;\n                for (int k = 0; k < 2; k++) {\n                    c[i][j] = (c[i][j] + a[i][k] * b[k][j]) % MOD;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return c;\n    }\n\n    private static long computeOdd(long base, long exp) {\n        return modPow(base, exp);\n    }\n\n    private static long modPow(long base, long exp) {\n        long res = 1;\n        base %= MOD;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) res = (res * base) % MOD;\n            base = (base * base) % MOD;\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class E {\n    static final long MOD = 998244353;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner in = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = in.nextLong();\n        long m = in.nextLong();\n        long L = in.nextLong();\n        long R = in.nextLong();\n        \n        long total = R - L + 1;\n        long odd = (L % 2 == 1) ? (total + 1) / 2 : total / 2;\n        long even = total - odd;\n        long cells = n * m;\n        \n        if ((n * m) % 2 == 0) {\n            System.out.println(computeEven(odd, even, cells));\n        } else {\n            System.out.println(computeOdd(odd, even, cells));\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static long computeEven(long odd, long even, long n) {\n        if (n == 0) return 1;\n        if (n == 1) return (odd + even) % MOD;\n        \n        long[][] trans = {{odd, even}, {even, odd}};\n        long[][] powered = matrixExp(trans, n);\n        return (powered[0][0] + powered[0][1] + powered[1][0] + powered[1][1]) % MOD;\n    }\n\n    private static long[][] matrixExp(long[][] base, long exp) {\n        long[][] result = {{1, 0}, {0, 1}};\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) result = matMul(result, base);\n            base = matMul(base, base);\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    private static long[][] matMul(long[][] a, long[][] b) {\n        long[][] c = new long[2][2];\n        for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < 2; j++) {\n                c[i][j] = 0;\n                for (int k = 0; k < 2; k++) {\n                    c[i][j] = (c[i][j] + a[i][k] * b[k][j]) % MOD;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return c;\n    }\n\n    private static long computeOdd(long odd, long even, long n) {\n        if (n == 0) return 1;\n        return (modPow(odd + even, n) + modPow(even - odd + MOD, n)) % MOD * modInverse(2) % MOD;\n    }\n\n    private static long modPow(long base, long exp) {\n        long res = 1;\n        base %= MOD;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) res = (res * base) % MOD;\n            base = (base * base) % MOD;\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    private static long modInverse(long a) {\n        return modPow(a, MOD - 2);\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.9\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.829164365422912e-05, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.396077979938127e-05, -8.4638240878121e-06, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -4.684815212385729e-05, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -3.099436753473128e-06, -0.029863232746720314, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, -1.311301275563892e-06, -2.264974000354414e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.768360213347478e-06, -1.07287787614041e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.4781842764932662e-05, -3.933898824470816e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -9.417489309271332e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -9.536697689327411e-06, -2.264974000354414e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -2.2649508537142538e-05